# Ingestion

Pipeline: fetch → snapshot → parse → extract → normalize → validate → candidate → (explicit) publish.

- Fetchers return bytes and HTTP metadata only.
- Parsers structure content. Extractors identify venues/deals/items.
- An LLM extractor later implements the same `Extractor` protocol. Do not fork the pipeline.
- Validators quarantine or reject. They do not write published deals.
- Publishers create/update consumer-visible rows and a `DealPublication` link.
- Network fetchers must use `ingestion/safety.py`: https-only (or http), DNS resolve, block private IPs, timeouts, size caps, robots.txt, source enable switch.
- Do not bypass auth, CAPTCHAs, or access controls. Do not scrape private content.
- Jobs are idempotent when practical. Use content hashes. Prefer `enqueue_source_refresh(source_id)`.
- Crawl failures must set `CrawlRun` error category/details and increment retry count. Never swallow exceptions.

```python
# ❌ BAD
deal = Deal(title=extracted.title, publication_state="published")
db.add(deal)

# ✅ GOOD
candidate = pipeline.ingest(source_id)  # stored, unpublished
publisher.publish(candidate_id, actor="admin")
```
